    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch12-16: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.80";
    dc:description "The universal prediction has a clear counterexample criterion and broad occurrence and phylogenetic data exist. Taxonomic uncertainty and sampling incompleteness reduce confidence but can be modeled.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Across pairs of regions, quantify counts of close phylogenetic replacements and test whether those counts predict shared species after controlling for area, distance and sampling. A reliably positive association supports the prediction; region pairs with many allied forms but no shared species refute its universal wording.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Species concepts and doubtful forms vary among taxonomic authorities.", "Unequal inventory effort creates false absences.";
